          "question": {
            "text": "Let $p, q, r$ be three logical statements. Consider the compound statements\n$S_1:((\\sim p) \\vee q) \\vee((\\sim p) \\vee r)$ and\n$S_2: p \\rightarrow(q \\vee r)$\nThen, which of the following is NOT true?",
